  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday night through Sunday)\nIssued at 229 AM EDT Mon Sep 28 2026\n\nWednesday and Thursday will be the final days with essentially \nzero PoPs for the week ahead. Thursday and Friday will bring an \namplifying a subtropical ridge over the Southeast and offshore \nover the western Atlantic. Meanwhile, moisture will increase as \nlow-/mid- level flow off of the Gulf and Atlantic spreads inland. \nThis setup will bring the return of isolated to scattered showers \nand storms Friday through Sunday. This synoptic pattern and AI NWP\nConvective Hazard Forecasts from NCAR continue to lack a signal \nfor severe weather potential. That said, the feed of tropical \nmoisture could favor an increasing heavy rainfall threat, as \nensemble guidance depicts PWAT reaching 1.8\" to 2.0\" over the \nweekend -- for context, the 90th percentile is 1.6\". The \nincreasing coverage of showers and storms will likely moderate \ntemperatures over the weekend, evidenced by progged highs in the \nmid-70s to lower 80s.",
